From 36fc43ea1cec22c2533e9e9b58b9d9cd8cdddc90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ryoma-89 <ryoma-89@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:21:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] velox: forward device-side acceleration structures and ray
 query (patch 0011)

Generated host code applies only the generator diff (KI-20). Builds arrive as
vkCmdBuildAccelerationStructuresFlatGOOGLE with the range infos flattened in
geometry order; the host rebuilds the pointer array after checking the counts
and that each geometry's data matches its type. Host-side acceleration
structure commands, indirect builds, capture/replay and update-after-bind are
masked and rejected, acceleration structures must fit their buffer, and
returned query data is zeroed. Unions are serialized by the active member's
sType, and union deep copies follow only the active member.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I0cdf463028b6d30ecd1c4e48dc5afcdb62b7ed0f
